Answer: done. A route may name `requires.stored`: `{"at": "<base id>", "item": "<item id>", "min": N}` or a list of them (commit a9fad22, test in scripts/tests/test_fleet_dispatch.py, failed before the change; game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md).
The dispatcher and fill.py send only a pilot whose own storage at that station holds `min` units or more by data/stock/storage.json (the service ledger reads each pilot about every 40 minutes), and not again until that storage was read after the pilot's last run of the route began: a carry takes the load out, and an old reading must not send the pilot twice.
The reason it gives the others: `stores N <item> at <base>, M wanted`, or `storage not read since its last run`.
Yours, as you planned: the withdraw stop of the circuit runner (scripts/fleet-build.sh) and the carry routes; `requires.bid` (below, ENT-125) can guard their sale end too.

